// D1602's CLAUSE-1 FACE, and the worst outcome class this repo grades: `vl check` rc 0, the
// module validates, the program exits 0, and it printed the WRONG VALUE. The call below goes
// through the closure-typed parameter `g`, which is what the checker resolved it to; the
// emitter resolved the callee by NAME first and called the module function instead.
//
// The parameter and the module function take the same argument count here, which is what
// makes this face silent rather than an arity mismatch inside `tak`. The wrong answer is 11
// and is deliberately not a superstring of the right one, since the grader's default
// contract is a substring test. The loud face is
// `tests/cases/closures/call-through-binding-shadowing-fn-name.vl`.
// Should print 8.
function g(x: i32) { print(x + 3) }

function tak(g: (i32) => void) { g(8) }

tak((n) => {
  print(n)
})
